# dist/ is deliberately NOT ignored — it is committed and served by Flask.
# The Pi has 1GB of RAM and no Node, so it never runs the build; see DEPLOY.md §3.
#
# It used to be listed here while its files were force-added, which meant a
# rebuild produced a new content-hashed bundle that git silently refused to
# stage. The result was an index.html referencing a script that was never
# committed — a white screen on the Pi, and nothing in the diff to explain it.
